WEBVTT

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.530
We’ll kidnap him.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:36.700
What?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.350
And then, we’ll spread the word that he’s been kidnapped.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.830
Once everyone hears about this scandal, he won’t be able to marry into any family.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.180
This will tarnish the family’s reputation quite a bit.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.540
Sounds interesting.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.480
I’d expect no less from a former thief.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.840
You catch on quickly.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.050
I’ll help, too.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.290
I’ll help with something as well.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.520
No, you won’t.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.930
But do you have a plan?

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.370
Will it just be the three of us?

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.810
There’s one more person who could be useful.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.280
Another former thief, eh?

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.600
So, you’re no longer working by yourself?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.790
I injured my arm, so I’m a bit worried.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.290
I used to be a robber, too.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.760
I quit in order to raise my daughter.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.300
How cute. All these bad boys together.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.870
Looks like that second son often takes strolls at night.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.640
I see you’ve already done some investigating.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.330
Maybe we should lure him with Otake.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.690
Take advantage of him being a pervert.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.900
And?

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.700
If this all works out, we will lock him up here.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.330
Here?

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.780
In the basement. There’s a room down there, right?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.480
I’m amazed you realized that.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.420
You can feel it when you walk.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.870
Well, I don’t go down there much.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.250
It’ll be fine.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.810
You can’t help but look at the floor, can you?

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.430
Keep an eye on the guy in the basement.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.160
Matsu is taking care of the mansion.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:56.040
He seems to be ignoring me.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.010
Well, he has always been a lone wolf. I guess that’s why.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.620
He doesn’t seem to like groups.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.730
Then, why did he join us?

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.510
No idea.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.410
Ichi.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.040
I don’t want any money.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.360
What do you want?

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.550
To beat him up and then dump him

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.320
in front of his future in-laws’ house.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.040
The exchange of money will happen soon.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.280
We will take the money, of course.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.040
We have to pay for the sleeping pills, and then there’s the hush money.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:36.500
Then, we will take some of it for ourselves,

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.510
and throw him in front of the house with the remaining money around his neck.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.010
All right, that sounds good.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.890
Returning
the hostage

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.310
M-Master!

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.350
I’m satisfied now.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.740
Thank you, people.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.730
That felt great.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:59.100
So, do you want to do it again?

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.740
This time for the money though.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.850
Isn’t it risky?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.840
We won’t be reckless enough to get caught.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.240
I’ll tag along in case you need help.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.810
I’ve decided to work for Ichi-san.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.000
I’m in as well. I want the money.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.760
So, we’ll need a name if we are going to keep doing this.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.180
Count me out.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.180
A mud turtle!

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.560
I thought I’d take it over to him.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:36.650
You mean to Masa?

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:37.400
Yeah.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.730
I’m closing the shop for today.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:46.950
I heard the feudal retainers in Edo are often affected by that disease...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.920
Though they seem to get cured when they return to their hometowns.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.450
Edo disease, huh?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:56.030
I guess I won’t get the chance to see whether or not he’s cut out for the bodyguard job.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.190
So, did he go back to his hometown?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.880
No, he said that wouldn’t be easy for him.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.250
So, he’s currently staying in the countryside on the outskirts of Edo.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.390
Well, seems to be better than being here.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.140
Have some gruel.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.860
Thank you.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.990
I’m really sorry for inconveniencing you.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.650
Forget about that and just concentrate on getting better.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.650
Anyway, I hope you get your appetite back.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:40.630
Have you officially joined the Five Leaves?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.630
You want the money, but you don’t want to do dirty jobs?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:52.960
I’m guessing that you’ll keep struggling with this dilemma,

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.890
but will help them out in the end.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:02.390
If you think the time has come to put an end to that dilemma, leave.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:03.620
That’s the best thing for you to do.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.570
Hey, Masa. You still alive?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.950
At this rate, he’s going to die from fatigue.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.450
I brought a mud turtle for you.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:19.420
Sorry you came all this way only to find that we’re closed.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:22.910
I don’t mind as long as I can have my drinks.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.030
Thanks, Matsu.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.750
It seems like Ume is a good Samaritan, too.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:31.430
He seems to like Masa-san.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.410
And is a bit overprotective of you.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:38.430
Well, as a child, I wasn’t very healthy.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.030
Maybe that’s why.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.760
What’s wrong?

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.700
I just remembered that I have a job to do.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:56.140
I wonder if he left because he doesn’t want to hear about Dad.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.120
I really wish they would get along.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.520
But Dad is always making unnecessary comments to him.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:07.380
Ume doesn’t hate people without a reason.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:11.540
That’s probably his way of reacting to Matsu’s attitude.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.640
You’re amazing, Otake-san.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.850
I’m sure he’ll cause a big fuss

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.130
when you tell him that you want to get married.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.390
I’ll go cut some pickles.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:34.500
In fact, the Five Leaves was established because he was overprotective of his daughter...

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:42.500
Here, eat some.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.000
I-I can’t.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.850
I brought it for you.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:50.660
I’ve had enough.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:55.080
The swelling in your legs won’t go away?

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:58.420
You sure it’s not because of the food you eat?

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.720
I don’t know.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.200
I bet you were only eating rice.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.750
Eat some vegetables.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.080
Beautiful weather today.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:11.010
He’s really a kind man.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.950
He used to be a big shot.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:17.200
He was the leader of a famous band of thieves,

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:20.200
and everyone admired him.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.910
You too?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.000
Yes. I used to be a member,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.890
though I was young and just a mere underling.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:33.010
Nevertheless, he even took care of someone like me.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:36.000
He’s like the Buddha to me.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.230
Even when you left them?

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:39.640
Yeah.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:42.500
Although I’m from Edo,

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.280
I was in China when I entered the band.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:48.120
I met a woman there, and then Kinu was born.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:52.650
She was a good-looking woman. Like Otake.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.660
But she passed away because of a disease.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:02.420
Just like her mother, Okinu wasn’t healthy.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.280
Thus, I had to raise her properly.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.630
So, I decided to quit the band.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.740
After I went to the old man about leaving, he talked with the other boss about it.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.560
Therefore, I was able to quit.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.270
When Okinu turned three, I went back to Edo

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.320
and opened that tavern.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.220
That’s really admirable, Ume-dono.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.260
Quit that.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.850
Go get some wood for the fire.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.250
You should get some exercise,

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.820
but take it easy.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.910
Shouldn’t we bring some tea to the old man and his guest?

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.630
He’ll leave soon.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.430
Do you know him as well?

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:13.810
One of his men?

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.940
He was my senior.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:19.830
I hope it’ll be all right.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.990
The mood seems to be tense.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.200
He comes over from time to time.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.930
Thanks for the help, Ume.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:45.510
Would you mind if I stop by your tavern?

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:51.220
You’re welcome... as a customer.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.370
Stop looking at me like that.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.830
Well...

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.290
Asking about everything is rude.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.740
I might talk about things I don’t want to when the alcohol kicks in,

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:16.890
but, unfortunately, there’s not a lot of that around here.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:24.980
I guess I can’t hate you since you ask me without realizing that it’s inconsiderate.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:32.060
Who’s this Yaichi guy?

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:35.480
He stops by my tavern quite often.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.060
Can we trust him?

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:42.920
No, but he doesn’t seem to be scheming about anything else either.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.340
It seems the other guys will provide their services if given another chance.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.080
Though I’m out.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:54.000
That’s for the best.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.950
Take this.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.630
I don’t want money.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.400
I’ve been in your care...

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.840
and, even now, I still am.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.340
Thanks to you, I was able to build a decent life.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:12.830
You won’t say something like “I don’t want dirty money.” right?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.310
That’s right.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.470
But you should keep that money.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.340
Senkichi-onii...

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.800
It’s been a while.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.470
So, you came to Edo as well.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.180
May I come in?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:14:00.780
You ran away from the gang with the money in your pocket.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.570
Why are you here now?

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.950
I left because you deserted me.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.610
I begged you to get me out of the band,

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:15.950
but you abandoned me.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:20.080
I had no other choice but to run away.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:25.590
The two leaders were Demon Spider Benzou and Buddha Souji.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.720
Just as the names imply, the Demon Spider brought the band together by his power,

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:34.600
and you were admired by your men for your virtue.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.450
We would always come to you first whenever there was a problem.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:42.460
That was a matter of course.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:48.860
I want to know why you didn’t talk to Demon Spider regarding my case.

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:53.870
You helped that brat get out of the band.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.840
He wasn’t useful, anyway.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.370
He was just tall, and that was it.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:02.870
Apparently, he’s living happily with his daughter.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.960
His life is the complete opposite of mine.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:12.340
It was impossible, even for me, to help two people leave the band within such a short period of time.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:16.260
But this goes without saying...

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:20.540
The band needed you as a lockpick.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.070
We couldn’t have let you go.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:27.990
But Ume was just a brat.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:30.610
It didn’t matter whether he was with us or not.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:35.180
Did you come all the way here to hear this?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.630
I want you to give me money.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:40.960
Money?

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.180
Thirteen years ago,

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:46.990
I promised a woman I met in a brothel that I would marry her.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.250
Therefore, I stole the money and paid for her debt.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:52.830
And then we ran away together.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:57.910
After much wandering, I opened a novelty shop in Edo.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:02.850
Then, he appeared.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.140
Denshichi?

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.070
Yes.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.690
A brat that used to be in the band.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:15.490
A few years later, after you retired, Demon Spider died, and the band split.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:20.320
I heard he’s working for someone else now.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.730
He’s threatening me to join them as a lockpick...

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.810
...by bringing up my past.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.010
But... I can’t do it anymore.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:36.760
My life isn’t the best, but I am happy.

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:41.770
I’ve got a daughter, too. I can’t dirty my hands.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:46.680
But if he talks to my old comrades,

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.770
and something happens to my daughter and wife...

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:54.910
He said that he hasn’t talked to anyone about me, yet.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.160
He’ll let me off the hook if I pay him.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:08.420
I heard talk that you were living here.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:11.610
There have been things I wanted to tell you, but I kept them to myself.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.840
You’re the only person I can turn to now.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.340
Please! Help me!

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.060
I have no money.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.560
Are you going to abandon me again?!

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.060
You are the one who broke the rules.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:34.530
You have to deal with the consequences yourself.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:22.470
Ume...

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.000
Thank you...

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.290
This won’t be the last time.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.550
I’ll come up with the money.

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:20.670
Don’t sympathize with him and take the burden.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:24.550
He doesn’t concern you, Ume.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.650
I want to do it.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.810
I won’t cause you any trouble.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:38.070
Are you going to dirty your hands by taking part in that band?

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:45.140
I grew up in that dirty world in the first place.

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:03.090
I wonder if Masa-san ate that mud turtle.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:15.740
I talk more than enough, even without being drunk.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:27.020
Don’t worry about that.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.080
You have to focus on getting better.

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:16.180
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:25.470
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:33.890
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:40.940
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:49.870
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:57.950
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:06.770
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:15.010
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:24.120
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:33.240
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:35.060
Madam here.

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:40.520
All the young girls do nothing but talk about men.

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:41.770
This is truly sad.

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:45.400
What’s going to happen to this country?

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:48.010
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:49.930
“Consider Yourself Lucky.”
